cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DocAssay, please cite this software using the metadata below. If a paper for this project is published later, prefer citing the paper in addition to or instead of the software release, as indicated by future updates to this file."
title: "DocAssay"
type: software

authors:
  - name: "center4aai"

version: "0.1.0"
license: "MIT"

abstract: >
  DocAssay is a local-first symbolic verifier of natural-language claims
  in repository documentation against a deterministic fact inventory, with
  explicit abstention (NEI). The verdict path is free of LLMs; LLM use is
  optional and limited to extraction fallback, never affecting a verdict. The
  same fact inventory is exposed to coding agents over the Model Context
  Protocol (and a Python API) as a deterministic source of truth.

keywords:
  - documentation verification
  - claim-evidence alignment
  - abstention
  - neuro-symbolic
  - deterministic analysis
  - fact verification
  - software documentation
  - source of truth
  - coding agents
  - model context protocol

date-released: 2026-08-29